# Career CV PDF Generator

The `/career` page generates a downloadable CV PDF from locale resume JSON + i18n UI labels.

## Architecture

| Piece | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Career UI | `src/components/Content/Career/CareerPage.tsx` |
| PDF builder | `src/utils/generateResumePdf.ts` |
| BY/RU button gate | `src/utils/resumeRegion.ts` |
| Resume fetch | `src/hooks/useResumeData.ts` → `/resume/resume.{locale}.json` |
| Types | `src/types/resume.ts` |
| Lazy route | `src/components/App/App.tsx` — `CareerPage` is `React.lazy` |

## pdfmake — CDN only

- Use **pdfmake 0.2.10 from cdnjs** inside `generateResumePdf.ts`
- Scripts load **only on generate button click**
- **Never** add `pdfmake` to `package.json` — it breaks CRA/React (duplicate React / hook errors)

```text
https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/pdfmake/0.2.10/pdfmake.min.js
https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/pdfmake/0.2.10/vfs_fonts.js
```

Roboto fonts from `vfs_fonts.js` support Cyrillic (RU) and Latin (EN).

## Generate flow

1. User locale (`en` | `ru`) selects JSON file and UI labels
2. `CareerPage` dynamically imports `generateResumePdf`
3. Resume data is **deep-cloned** before building the document
4. Photo fetched from `personal.photoUrl` → base64 data URL
5. pdfmake creates PDF; filename: `CV-{name}-{locale}.pdf`

## pdfmake mutation rule (critical)

pdfmake **mutates** `ul` arrays in the doc definition (strings become internal layout objects).

**Always:**
- Clone resume data: `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(data))`
- Copy arrays: `ul: job.highlights.map((item) => String(item))`
- Never pass references from React state / fetched JSON directly into pdfmake

If skipped, React re-render throws: `Objects are not valid as a React child`.

## Photo

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| JSON | `personal.photoUrl` → `/resume/avatar.jpg` |
| File | `public/resume/avatar.jpg` |
| Source copy | `src/assets/images/avatar.jpg` (homepage avatar) |

To change CV photo: replace `public/resume/avatar.jpg` or update `photoUrl` in both locale JSON files.

PDF layout: portrait photo in header — `fit: [68, 118]` (keeps aspect ratio, not squashed).

## Buttons

### Generate CV (PDF)
- Always visible
- i18n: `career.downloadPdf`, `career.generatingPdf`, `career.generatePdfError`
- Builds PDF from current locale data

### Download rabota.by CV
- Visible only when `hasBelarusRussiaWorkPermit(personal.workPermit)` is true
- Both Belarus **and** Russia must appear in workPermit (supports `Belarus`/`Беларусь`, `Russia`/`Россия`)
- Links to `personal.pdfUrl` (`/resume/FM-resume.pdf`)
- i18n: `career.downloadLocalPdf`

## PDF content sections

Header (with photo) → About → Work experience → Skills → Languages → Education → Courses → Additional → Updated date footer.

Section titles use i18n (`ResumePdfLabels` passed from `CareerPage`).

## When to edit code vs JSON

| Change | Action |
|--------|--------|
| Job text, skills, contacts | Edit `resume.ru.json` + `resume.en.json` only |
| New resume field | Update `src/types/resume.ts`, JSON files, `CareerPage` render, `generateResumePdf.ts` if needed in PDF |
| New PDF section | Edit `generateResumePdf.ts` + i18n labels |
| New UI button/label | Edit `CareerPage.tsx` + `en.ts` / `ru.ts` |
| Change photo file | Replace `public/resume/avatar.jpg` |

## Verify

```bash
pnpm dev   # /career — switch RU/EN, generate PDF, check photo + no React errors after download
pnpm build
```
